Talking about new ideas to Nethack, how about these:

1) More multicharacter animals (like long worms). For example, a large
  animal might be sized 2*2 characters; different parts of the monster
  would fight diffrently (think about that huge tail of the dragon,
  it would not breathe fire but would slay you down easily).
  There's a problem, though: it seems large monsters wouldn't be able
  to go into narrow corridors.

2) Plants. Apple trees, for example. These would probably be like monsters
  except that they wouldn't move or attack you; you couldn't kill them
  either, at least not easily (AC -100, HP 1000). However, you can kick
  an apple tree and apples might fall on the ground. There could also
  be demons living in the trees and they wouldn't like kicking.
  You can cut a tree down with a saw or an axe, though I don't know
  what use you could have for the tree then. You could also talk to
  the trees to detect if there is a demon living in it (?).

3) Sleep. Would be refreshing and maybe you would *have* to sleep from
  time to time, otherwise you get too tired. You could have dreams,
  ie. you would enter a special dream dungeon. Your characteristics
  and inventory items would be different from those you have when awake.
  You might learn spells or gain intrinsics, however, that wouldn't
  vanish when you wake up.
  You might even have nightmares, running away from a *big* monster
  and finally waking up when it gets you.
